 "finish_summary": "Explored three RTL variants of the 32-bit registered adder `addpipe32`: (1) the original straightforward `a_i + b_i` with valid-gated register, (2) a manually split 16-bit carry-select adder aiming to shorten the critical path, and (3) an explicit 32-bit Kogge-Stone parallel-prefix adder aiming for O(log N) logic depth. Both restructured versions actually performed worse post-route (carry-select: area 738.68 um\u00b2, WNS 7.349 ns, score 72.75; Kogge-Stone: area 754.11 um\u00b2, WNS 7.457 ns, score 73.82) than the original simple design (area 746.13 um\u00b2, WNS 7.487 ns, score 74.126), confirmed reproducible via resubmission. This shows Yosys/ABC's default synthesis combined with OpenROAD placement/routing already produces a near-optimal, low-area, low-delay ripple-carry-based implementation for this small adder, and manual RTL-level restructuring only added overhead without any measurable timing benefit after physical implementation. The best verified result is the original RTL with score 74.126 (area 746.13 um\u00b2, WNS 7.48722 ns), which is retained as the final submission.",
